---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { getContactLinks } from "../lib/site-content";

const contact = await getContactLinks();
const EFFECTIVE_DATE = "23 September 2026";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Sunflora"
  description="How Sunflora collects, uses and protects your personal data, and your rights under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023."
  effectiveDate={EFFECTIVE_DATE}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Privacy Policy</Fragment>

  <p>
    Sunflora ("Sunflora", "we", "us", "our") is a home-based, handmade crochet
    studio operated by Aru Jaiswal, based in Siwan, Bihar, India. Sunflora is
    not a separately registered company — it trades simply as "Sunflora".
    This policy explains what personal data we collect through
    sunfloracrochet.in (the "Site"), why we collect it, who we share it with,
    and the rights you have over it under the Digital Personal Data
    Protection Act, 2023 ("DPDP Act") and other applicable Indian law.
  </p>
  <p>
    Under the DPDP Act, Sunflora acts as the <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong>
    and you, as a visitor or customer, are the <strong>Data Principal</strong>.

  </p>

  <h2>1. What personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>We collect personal data directly from you, in these situations:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Creating an account or signing in</strong> — your name and
      email address (we use passwordless "magic link" sign-in, so we never
      ask for or store a password).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Placing an order</strong> — your name, phone number, email
      address, and delivery address (address line(s), city, state and
      pincode), plus order notes you choose to add.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Custom order requests and the contact form</strong> — your
      name, email, and whatever details, reference images or links you
      choose to share about the piece you'd like made.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Product reviews</strong> — your name and the content of the
      review you submit, which is displayed publicly on the product page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Payments</strong> — we do <strong>not</strong> collect or store
      your card, UPI or bank details. Payments are processed directly by our
      payment gateway, Razorpay; we only receive the order amount, payment
      status and a transaction reference.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Automatically</strong> — standard technical data such as your
      approximate location (from IP address), browser/device type, and pages
      visited, collected by our hosting and security provider. Your cart
      contents are kept only in your browser's local storage until you check
      out — see our <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not knowingly collect any special or sensitive category of
    personal data (such as health, financial account, or biometric data)
    beyond what is described above.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Why we use your data</h2>
  <p>We use your personal data only for the purposes you'd reasonably expect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>to process, pack, ship and deliver your order;</li>
    <li>to communicate with you about your order, custom request, or enquiry;</li>
    <li>to create and manage your account and order history;</li>
    <li>to respond to customer support requests and resolve issues;</li>
    <li>to display product reviews you've chosen to submit;</li>
    <li>
      to maintain the security, integrity and proper functioning of the
      Site;
    </li>
    <li>
      to comply with tax, accounting and consumer-protection obligations
      under Indian law; and
    </li>
    <li>
      with your separate consent only, to send you updates, offers or
      marketing communications, and to measure how the Site is used (see our
      <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data, and we do not use it for any purpose
    beyond what is described in this policy without asking you first.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Consent</h2>
  <p>
    By creating an account, placing an order, submitting the contact form,
    or otherwise providing your personal data to us, you consent to it being
    processed as described in this policy. Where processing is not
    necessary to fulfil your order or a legal obligation — such as
    analytics or marketing — we ask for your consent separately (through the
    cookie preference banner) and you may withdraw it at any time without
    affecting orders already placed. Withdrawing consent for data that is
    genuinely necessary to complete an order you've placed may mean we're
    unable to fulfil that order.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Who we share your data with</h2>
  <p>
    We share personal data only with service providers who help us run the
    Site and fulfil your order, under obligations to keep it secure and use
    it only for the purpose we've engaged them for:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Supabase</strong> — our database, authentication and
      file-storage provider. Your account, order and address data is stored
      on Supabase's infrastructure.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Razorpay</strong> — our payment gateway, which processes
      payments directly and securely; we never see your full card or bank
      details.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — our hosting and content-delivery
      provider.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Courier and logistics partners</strong> — to whom we pass your
      name, phone number and delivery address solely to ship your order.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose personal data if required to do so by law, court
    order, or a valid request from a government or regulatory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Where your data is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Some of our service providers (including Supabase and Cloudflare) may
    process or store data on servers located outside India. Where this
    happens, we rely on those providers' own security and contractual
    safeguards. As of the effective date above, the Central Government has
    not notified any country to which transfer of personal data is
    restricted under Section 16 of the DPDP Act.
  </p>

  <h2>6. How long we keep your data</h2>
  <p>
    We retain personal data only for as long as reasonably necessary for
    the purposes described in this policy — for example, order and invoice
    records are kept for as long as required under applicable Indian tax
    and accounting law. Account data is retained until you ask us to delete
    it, subject to any legal retention obligations that still apply (such
    as completed order records).
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights as a Data Principal</h2>
  <p>Under the DPDP Act, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Access</strong> a summary of the personal data we hold about
      you and how it has been processed;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Correct or update</strong> inaccurate or incomplete personal
      data;
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Erase</strong> personal data that is no longer necessary for
      the purpose it was collected for;
    </li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, as easily as you gave it;</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Nominate</strong> another individual to exercise these rights
      on your behalf in the event of your death or incapacity; and
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Grievance redressal</strong> — raise a complaint about how we
      handle your personal data (see below).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact our Grievance Officer using the
    details in Section 10. We'll acknowledge your request promptly and
    respond within a reasonable time, consistent with the DPDP Act and its
    rules.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children's data</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is not directed at children. Under the DPDP Act, a "child" is
    anyone under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal data from a child
    without verifiable consent of their parent or lawful guardian. If you
    believe a child has provided us with personal data without such
    consent, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. How we protect your data</h2>
  <p>
    We use reasonable technical and organisational safeguards to protect
    your personal data — including encrypted (HTTPS) connections, access
    controls, and database-level row security restricting who can read or
    write your data. No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure,
    but we work to protect your data appropriately for what it is.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Grievance Officer</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a question, complaint, or wish to exercise any right
    described above, please contact:
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Aru Jaiswal</strong> (Grievance Officer)<br />
    Sunflora, Siwan, Bihar, India<br />
    Email: <a href={contact.mailto}>{contact.email}</a><br />
    WhatsApp: <a href={contact.whatsappUrl}>{contact.phoneDisplay}</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    If you're not satisfied with how we've resolved your grievance, you may
    approach the Data Protection Board of India under the DPDP Act.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time — for example, as our use of
    analytics or marketing tools changes. We'll post the revised policy here
    with an updated effective date, and, where the change is material,
    we'll make reasonable efforts to bring it to your attention.
  </p>

  <hr />
  <p>
    See also our <a href="/terms-and-conditions">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>
    and <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
